---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { formatPagePath } from '../lib/urls';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Supported Formats and Current Limits - LocalResizer"
  description="See the current public formats, live page types, and feature limits for LocalResizer."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase mb-3">Public Scope</span>
      <h1 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 tracking-tight mb-4">Supported formats and current limits</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        This page explains what the live public version of LocalResizer supports today, what each page family does, and which workflows are intentionally out of scope for now.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-12">
      <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 shadow-soft border border-stone-100">
        <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">Supported image formats</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>JPEG</strong> for photo-heavy compression, target-size workflows, and JPG conversion output</li>
          <li><strong>PNG</strong> for graphics, transparent images, and PNG conversion output</li>
          <li><strong>WebP</strong> for modern static image resizing, compression, and supported converter input</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 shadow-soft border border-stone-100">
        <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">Current public page types</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Homepage quick tool</strong> for compressing by file size or resizing by dimensions</li>
          <li><strong>Batch resize page</strong> for applying one bounding size to as many as 20 static images</li>
          <li><strong>Target-size pages</strong> such as 50 KB, 100 KB, 200 KB, and 2 MB workflows</li>
          <li><strong>Exact canvas pages</strong> for the currently live social artwork workflows</li>
          <li><strong>Format converter pages</strong> for WebP to JPG and JPG or WebP photo to PNG</li>
          <li><strong>Specialized utility pages</strong> for signature cleanup and grid-based image splitting</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="border-y border-stone-200 py-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-5">Convert between the supported formats</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">WebP input, JPG output</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
            When a destination rejects WebP but accepts JPEG, <a href={formatPagePath('webp-to-jpg')} class="text-teal-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-teal-900">convert WebP to JPG</a> with a chosen quality and background for transparent areas.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">JPG or WebP input, PNG output</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
            When an editor or upload form requires PNG, <a href={formatPagePath('photo-to-png')} class="text-teal-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-teal-900">convert a JPG or WebP photo to PNG</a> while keeping its pixel dimensions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 shadow-soft border border-stone-100 mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">What the current live pages actually guarantee</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Compress pages</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">They aim for a target file-size budget locally. JPEG and WebP use quality search, while PNG pages keep PNG output and may reduce dimensions if needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Resize-to-size pages</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">They reduce image dimensions toward a smaller file-size budget while preserving the original aspect ratio and keeping already-small files unchanged.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Exact canvas pages</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">They export an exact output canvas for the live platform sizes, keep the whole image visible, and may add padding when the image ratio does not match.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Format converter pages</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">They re-encode one static image to a locked JPG or PNG output, preserve pixel dimensions, and may change file size or remove source metadata.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Specialized utility pages</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">They cover focused workflows such as trimming and resizing signature images or splitting a static image into a simple grid of downloadable tiles.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Batch resize page</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">It applies one width and height bounding box to multiple files, preserves each aspect ratio, keeps the original format, and offers a ZIP download.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 shadow-soft border border-stone-100 mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">Current limits and unsupported workflows</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li>Animated GIF workflows are not part of the current public release.</li>
        <li>Animated WebP is not supported by the current format converter pages.</li>
        <li>Video processing is not part of the current public release.</li>
        <li>Target-size workflows are best-effort because exact output depends on the source image.</li>
        <li>Batch selections are limited to 20 files and 100MB total, with additional source-image and output-canvas pixel limits.</li>
        <li>The live platform pages do not auto-crop and do not generate alternate social-media safe-area variants.</li>
        <li>All current public workflows are browser-based and do not require an account.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-7 shadow-soft border border-stone-100 mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-4">Guide pages that explain the live tool set</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
        <a href={formatPagePath('compress-image')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Compress Image Guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Compare the current live compression pages and understand how JPEG and PNG behave differently.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('resize-image')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Resize Image Guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">See how the live resize-by-size pages work and which target-size page best matches your upload limit.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('youtube-image-sizes')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">YouTube Image Size Guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Review the current YouTube banner and thumbnail pages when you need a YouTube fixed canvas.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('image-tools')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Image Tools Guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Open the live converter, signature, and image-splitting workflows from one guide.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('why-image-size-is-best-effort')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Why target size is best-effort</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Understand why target-size pages aim for a budget instead of guaranteeing the same exact byte count on every source image.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('jpeg-vs-png-vs-webp-for-upload-limits')} class="no-underline rounded-xl border border-stone-100 bg-stone-50/70 p-5 hover:border-teal-200 hover:bg-teal-50/40 transition-all">
          <h3 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">JPEG vs PNG vs WebP guide</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Choose the right current format when upload size, transparency, and compatibility all pull in different directions.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="text-center">
      <h2 class="font-[var(--font-heading)] text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Need more detail?</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">
        For privacy details, visit the privacy page. For questions, bug reports, or feature requests, use the contact page.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href={formatPagePath('privacy')} class="inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2.5 bg-white border border-stone-200 text-stone-600 text-sm font-medium rounded-xl no-underline hover:border-teal-300 hover:text-teal-700 hover:bg-teal-50 transition-all duration-200">Privacy</a>
        <a href={formatPagePath('contact')} class="inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2.5 bg-white border border-stone-200 text-stone-600 text-sm font-medium rounded-xl no-underline hover:border-teal-300 hover:text-teal-700 hover:bg-teal-50 transition-all duration-200">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
